# Allowlist: ignore everything by default, then explicitly un-ignore only
# what main.py needs at runtime. A new file the runtime needs must be added here explicitly too, or the
# image builds fine but fails at runtime -- fail loud, not fail quiet.
#
# NOTE: config.yaml is intentionally NOT included -- it's injected at
# runtime via docker-compose's `configs:` mount (see docker-compose.yml)
# or, in Cloud Run, mounted from the GCS bucket (see README.md).
*

!main.py
!requirements.txt
!source
!source/**
!models
!models/**

# Rules below apply AFTER the negations above (last-match-wins), so they
# re-exclude compiled bytecode that would otherwise ride along inside the
# allowed source/ tree.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
